Individual Contributions
- Code: 
  - Data exploration and wrangling for covariates that would be most appropriate to showcase heatmap functionality. 
  - Focusing on categorical covariates of age and education, along with a categorical output of household income, I created several heatmaps to showcase patterns between the inputs and output.
  - For the covariate age, I created plots using age by decade, age by month, and continuous age, before sticking to the first and last for ease of user interpretability in the heatmaps. 
  - Creation of facets by gender, race, and both gender and race to better view patterns within each category.
  - Creation of shiny shell (ui and server) for user interactivity and heatmap output, respectively.
  - Creation of hover functionality using shiny, which outputs the data in each heatmap datapoint when users hover over the heatmap.
- Final Report: 
  - I wrote the initial paragraphs of the methods section, describing the data exploration, wrangling, coding, and shiny app creation.
  - For the methods, results, and discussion section, I wrote in depth explanations regarding the creation, key findings, and trend interpretations from the heatmaps. 
